      "solution": "N = int(input())\nK = int(input())\n\nfor _ in range(K):\n    if N % 2 == 0:\n        N //= 2\n    else:\n        N = N * 3 + 1\n\nprint(N)",
      "statement": "You are given a starting integer [[N]].\nYou must transform [[N]] using a sequence of logical rules and output the final result.\n\nThe transformation works as follows:\n\n1. If [[N]] is {{even}}, divide it by 2.\n2. If [[N]] is {{odd}}, multiply it by 3 and add 1.\n3. Repeat steps 1–2 exactly [[K]] times.\n4. At the end, output the final value of [[N]].\n\nYour task is to simulate this process and print the result after exactly [[K]] steps.",
